# An opaque reference given under a free name its reader uses as a typed reference is admitted as the explicit
# analogue is (RECEPTION-EDGE-DEBTS (e); Codex: "the same receiving-edge conversion/admission as the explicit
# analogue, provided actual reference depth/type is correct").  observe reads shared\value, the unit declares
# `@: Model shared`, relay only hands the name on, and caller binds it to its opaque p.  A Model: 11.  An Other,
# whose `value` is its second field: 9, by name.  A Thin, which has no `value`: refused where caller forms relay's
# input, taken by caller's handler, 42.  Until 2026-10-05 caller's call of relay was refused at translation,
# "incompatible entry signature".  Entry 7.
Model: (size_t: value 11U)
Other:
    size_t: pad 1U
    size_t: value 9U
end: Other
Thin: (int: pad 1)
@: Model shared @Model
fn: observe () size_t
return: shared\value
fn: relay () size_t
return: observe()
fn: caller (@: void p) size_t
    size_t: r 0U
    @: void shared p
    r: relay()
    catch: implements ()
        r: 42U
    ---
return: r
wide: merge: Other
bad: merge: Thin
size_t: a caller(@Model)
size_t: b caller(wide)
size_t: c caller(bad)
int: ok 7
if: a != 11U
    ok: 81
if: b = 1U
    ok: 61
if: b != 9U && b != 1U
    ok: 82
if: c != 42U
    ok: 83
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
